WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.320
This piece "Lagrima" by Francisco Tarrega, is a classical guitar&nbsp;
standard and "Lagrima" of course means&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:13.020
teardrop. So it should be sad, right? And&nbsp;
there are some sad moments but actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:20.340
most of the piece is in major. This key,&nbsp;
E major. It's only in the second section&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:29.160
that we get the minor key, which is usually&nbsp;
associated with sadness. Minor Keys sound sad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:37.920
and major keys sound happy. So I thought it'd&nbsp;
be fun to invert the keys of Lagrima. Instead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:46.120
of playing in E Major, play in E minor and&nbsp;
then the B section:instead of playing in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:53.520
the minor key, what happens if&nbsp;
we play in major? Let's find out!

